As I said, the bug is in the runtime. This should not throw with redirected standard output, but does:

```
NativeMethods.FreeConsole();
Console.OutputEncoding = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8;
Console.WriteLine("Output CP = " + NativeMethods.GetConsoleOutputCP());
```

I stuck `NativeMethods.FreeConsole();` on the top because the reproduction is difficult otherwise, but it is possible. The wine setup is giving you something more like `ssh hostname dotnet --version` instead of `dotnet --version`. Your console process doesn't have a console yet.

Run the attached project with `dotnet run > log 2> log2` and the exception appears in log2.

[r38613.zip](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/files/14284339/r38613.zip)

Calling SetConsoleOutputCP() for a redirected handle is a bug even when it doesn't crash. It will mess up the caller's console by changing the glyph mappings. Call `isatty` first to check for redirected standard output/error.
